                            <comment id="14747033" author="githubbot" created="Wed, 16 Sep 2015 07:09:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user corneadoug commented on the pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/309#issuecomment-140650954&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/309#issuecomment-140650954&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    I always thought this feature should be done using RestApi so that you don&apos;t get any websocket message, but this is somehow working without any problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    However the event we rely on in this PR is pretty much not needed originally.&lt;br/&gt;
    `` broadcastNote(newNote);`` should not be called in the case of a createNewNote or CopyNote.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14995308" author="githubbot" created="Sat, 7 Nov 2015 17:30:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user Leemoonsoo commented on the pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/309#issuecomment-154726309&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/309#issuecomment-154726309&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    I think it&apos;s okay to use websocket, while this implementation does not adds more complexity (ie. new websocket message) and it&apos;s more consistent to keep using websocket for notebook operations in webapp.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
